---
/* Site-wide footer — brief §4 requires the newsletter signup on every page.
   Before this port, home.html and conference.html each carried their own
   copy, and conference's had drifted: it never received the mobile
   rounded-card rework (15 Sept) that home's did. One component now, so
   that gap can't reopen. */
---
<footer class="ft g-paper" id="footer">

  <!-- register 1: the dense ruled grid -->
  <div class="ft__grid">
    <div class="ft__cell ft__cell--news">
      <p class="ft__k">Newsletter</p>
      <p class="ft__lead">Occasional notes on what the tribe is making.<br>No spam, no sermons.</p>
      <form class="ft__form" onsubmit="event.preventDefault(); this.dataset.sent='1';">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="nl">Email address</label>
        <input id="nl" type="email" placeholder="you@email.com" autocomplete="email" required>
        <button type="submit" aria-label="Join the newsletter">→</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="ft__linkcols">
      <nav class="ft__cell" aria-label="Site">
        <p class="ft__k">Site</p>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/conference">No Bushels</a>
        <a href="/work">Our work</a>
      </nav>

      <!-- 29 Oct, client note: real social URLs. X's given URL was
           identical to Facebook's (facebook.com/TheGlowTribe), almost
           certainly a copy-paste slip -- left unlinked rather than
           guessing at the real one. target="_blank" is new here too:
           these were "#" placeholders before, never real external
           destinations. -->
      <nav class="ft__cell" aria-label="Elsewhere">
        <p class="ft__k">Elsewhere</p>
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/theglowtribe_/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@theglowtribeng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube</a>
        <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@theglowtribe_" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TikTok</a>
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/TheGlowTribe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook</a>
        <a href="#">X</a>
        <a href="#">Email</a>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <!-- 29 Oct, client note: merch is live now -- real link, not a
         "soon" tag, and the column heading changes from "Soon" since
         it's no longer true of everything in it. -->
    <div class="ft__cell">
      <p class="ft__k">More</p>
      <a href="/shop/all">Merch</a>
      <span class="ft__soon">Blog</span>
      <span class="ft__soon">Opportunities</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- register 2: the wordmark whole and full-bleed.
       The embedded countdown is GONE — a day-count in a footer is meaningless
       out of context, and it was there to satisfy the seed rather than the
       page. The seed's "numeral inside letterforms" reading is served instead
       by 5:15 — the verse the whole event is named after, and the one
       colon-numeral the brand is allowed. It means something here; 69 did not. -->
  <div class="ft__mark" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="ft__word">Glow Tribe</span>
  </div>
</footer>
